tests/golden/slang — the v1.1.0 SystemVerilog adapter's gate golden

alwaysblock2.blif is the gate-mapped netlist of
tests/unit/data/slang/verilog-eval/Prob058_alwaysblock2_ref.sv through

  read_techlib lib/cmos6.o3lib
  read_verilog Prob058_alwaysblock2_ref.sv        (the slang adapter)
  proc; opt; lower; abc --gates cmos6; dfflibmap cmos6
  write_blif --gates-as-names alwaysblock2.blif

run by tests/cli/slang_flow.sh (CTest cli_slang_flow), which also proves the structural Verilog
of every fixture reads back equivalent. The BLIF is deterministic for the ABC pin (a3001b72) and
cmos6; it records that the adapter, the gate flow and the writer together do not drift. The
fixture is NVIDIA verilog-eval's (MIT; see tests/unit/data/slang/verilog-eval/NOTICE).
